  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently VRChat does not support custom NavMesh areas.  There are only Walkable, Nonwalkable, and Jump areas.  It is possible to set the costs of these layers at runtime to use one or more of them as a very basic differentiated mesh, but if you want any other sort of complex AI navigation, the custom areas are not supported.  \nExample: you have terrain with large stones.  The AI needs to be able to get up on the stones in some cases, but it looks very odd for the AI to run directly up and over them in regular pathfinding.  If you can set the stones to a custom layer with a higher cost, the pathfinding will prefer to route around these obstacles.  \nhttps://docs.unity3d.com/460/Documentation/Manual/NavLayersAndCosts.html",
